  "answer": "This feature has been requested before. PowerToys has no timed shutdown or sleep tool. The maintainers closed the duplicate requests in favor of PowerToys#28490, which is the main ticket for a scheduled shutdown, sleep or restart utility. You can follow it there and add a thumbs-up. Until it exists, use the built-in Windows command. Press Win+R and run `shutdown /s /t N`, where N is the number of seconds. For example, `shutdown /s /t 1800` shuts down after 30 minutes. `shutdown /a` cancels it. `shutdown /i` opens a dialog. You can also put the command in a shortcut or trigger it from Task Scheduler. The `shutdown` command has no sleep option, so sleep needs a different approach, such as a scheduled task."
 },
